# Limitations

1. **Access, the largest limitation.** {{n_in_scope_no_fulltext}} papers that meet the criteria on their abstracts ({{pct_lost_to_access}}% of all in-scope papers) had no full text retrievable by this pipeline: they are not in Europe PMC's open-access XML, and publisher sites were not reachable from the build environment. They include central studies on visible-light depolymerization of commercial polymethacrylates, PET-RAFT depolymerization, poly(vinyl ether) upcycling and several polystyrene photo-oxidation systems. v1.0 is therefore a verified sample of the open literature, biased toward journals that deposit in PubMed Central, not a census. They are listed (code E6) in `data/curated/screening_log.csv` for v1.1.
2. **AI curation.** An independent AI audit of the release candidate (two rounds) found screening miscodes and several attribution problems (conditions or values taken from a different experiment in the same paper), all since corrected; it found no wrong numbers in an 18-record sample. Screening, extraction, verification and harmonization decisions were made by an AI system under the author's delegation; no human expert reviewed individual records. Deterministic checks guarantee that each number is printed at its cited location; correct attribution to the experiment relies on independent AI re-extraction and adjudication.
3. **Text and tables only.** Values shown only in figures or supplementary files were not recorded ({{n_excluded_observations}} observations listed with reasons). Molar-mass time courses, in particular, are mostly in figures.
4. **Small and uneven.** {{n_records_released}} records from {{n_included_papers}} papers; polystyrene dominates ({{by_polymer}}).
5. **Conventional SEC is relative.** Calibration classes: {{by_calibration_class}}. Absolute cross-paper comparison of molar masses is approximate.
6. **Light dose not harmonized.** Most papers report electrical lamp power or colour, not irradiance or photon flux at the sample.
7. **Heat as co-driver.** Thermal regimes: {{by_thermal_regime}}. In at least one system a dark control at the same temperature gives most of the lit result; such records are flagged.
8. **Approximate values and conditions read from elsewhere in a paper.** QA flags: {{qa_flag_counts}}. Values printed as approximate are recorded as printed and flagged. Conditions read from a different paragraph or table than the result (typically a paper's own "standard conditions" statement) are flagged as `conditions_from_other_block`.
9. **Publication bias.** Positive results are reported more than failures; controls are kept but the benchmark over-represents successful conditions.
10. **Scope conventions.** Photothermal routes and photoreforming after chemical pretreatment were excluded (E4); this is escalated to the author and may change in later versions.
